This instance runs FetchDock, open-source software that downloads media from websites when its users ask it to. This policy explains which personal data the instance processes, why, for how long, and who can see it.

FetchDock generated this policy from a list of everything the software stores and sends (kept in sync with the code by automated tests), from this instance's configuration, and from the operator's answers. The operator adopted it as the privacy policy of this instance.

## Who is responsible

The controller for your personal data on this instance is {{ a.operator.name ?? missing }}{% if a.operator.address is not null %}, {{ a.operator.address|replace({"\n": ', '}) }}{% endif %}.

{% if a.operator.contactEmail is not null %}
Contact: [{{ a.operator.contactEmail }}](<mailto:{{ a.operator.contactEmail|e('markdown_url')|raw }}>)
{% else %}
Contact: {{ missing }}
{% endif %}

{% if a.operator.dpoContact is not null %}
Data protection officer: {{ a.operator.dpoContact }}
{% endif %}

The FetchDock developers do not operate this instance and receive no personal data from it{% if config.failureReports.forwarding is not null %}, except the problem reports you choose to forward (see "Problem reports"){% endif %}.

## Legal basis

{% if a.legalBasis == 'contract' %}
The instance processes your data to provide the download service you signed up for (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR).
{% elseif a.legalBasis == 'legitimate_interest' %}
The instance processes your data on the basis of the operator's legitimate interest in providing the download service to the people they admitted, and in keeping it secure and working (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). You can object to it (see "Your rights").
{% else %}
{{ missing }}
{% endif %}

Problem reports are only sent when you choose to send one.

## What the instance stores

You sign in through the instance's identity provider. The instance stores the following data about you in its database.

{% for category, items in inventory.categories %}
### {{ categoryLabels[category] ?? category }}

{% for item in items %}
- **{{ item.summary }}.** Purpose: {{ item.purposes|join('; ') }}. Kept {% for retention in item.retentions %}{{ retentionLabels[retention] ?? retention }}{{ loop.last ? '' : '; ' }}{% endfor %}. Visible to {% for audience in item.audiences %}{{ audienceLabels[audience] ?? audience }}{{ loop.last ? '' : ', ' }}{% endfor %}.
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}
"Visible to" describes access through the app. Administrators can see your account identifier and the downloads of all users{% if config.viewAllRoleHolders %}, and so can other users the operator allowed to view all downloads{% endif %}. People with direct access to the server or its database, such as the operator and the hosting provider, can technically see all data.

## Data outside the database

{% for entry in inventory.storage %}
- **{{ entry.what }}.** Where: {{ entry.where }}. Purpose: {{ entry.purpose }}. Kept {{ retentionLabels[entry.retention] ?? entry.retention }}.{% if entry.notes is not null %} {{ entry.notes }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}

## How long data is kept

There is no self-service account deletion: to have your account and data deleted, contact the operator. You can delete your downloads, settings, apps and problem reports yourself.

Deleting a download job hides it, but does not erase it, and the downloaded files stay on disk while other users or the operator keep them.
{% if a.retention.softDeletedJobsDays is not null %}
The operator erases deleted download jobs after {{ a.retention.softDeletedJobsDays }} days.
{% endif %}
{% if a.retention.reportsDays is not null %}
The operator deletes problem reports after {{ a.retention.reportsDays }} days.
{% endif %}
{% if a.retention.logsDays is not null %}
Logs are kept for {{ a.retention.logsDays }} days.
{% else %}
How long logs are kept: {{ missing }}
{% endif %}
{% if a.retention.backups is not null %}
Backups: {{ a.retention.backups }}
{% endif %}

